                <pb facs="0233" n="139" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg139"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00 R 296/522: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kellogg</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-08-19T13:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 19,
                                1924—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 19—8:38
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>359. Young canceled his sailing reservations for tomorrow. He will go to Paris
                    and work out plan of reparations as Agent General. I think that it will be
                    arranged to carry out your original program for his temporary appointment to
                    start the Dawes Plan in operation. He hopes that arrangement as to permanent
                    Agent General may be reached as soon as possible.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
